# modelSpell — operating rules

1. Work only in `.venv`: `python3 -m venv .venv`, activate it,
   `python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'`. Never use system or conda Python; run
   `python -m pytest`, never bare `pytest`. Never commit `.venv/` or a real API key.
2. Keep audiences separate: `README.md` for users, `DEVEL.md` for maintenance,
   `NEWS.md` for the changelog. Update `DEVEL.md` in the same change whenever layout,
   commands, tests, UI, release steps or workflow permissions change.
3. `NEWS.md` records user-visible changes only: one bullet of at most 20 words under
   the version in `modelspell/_version.py`. Released sections are immutable. Tests,
   docs, UI, scripts and CI changes need no entry and no version bump.
4. `modelspell/_version.py` is the only version source. Bump it on `devel` before any
   change to `modelspell/`, `pyproject.toml`, `README.md` or `LICENSE` reaches `main`,
   and run `python scripts/build_release.py --smoke` before merging.
5. The wheel ships only `modelspell/**`, metadata and `LICENSE`. Keep the hatch
   `packages` and sdist `only-include` lists restrictive; packaging or metadata changes
   must keep `scripts/build_release.py` verification and K3/K7 green.
6. `tests.yml` keeps the 3.10/3.13 matrix and `workflow_call`; `release.yml` keeps
   `contents: write`, its concurrency group, NEWS-derived notes and the sha256 install
   line. Verify an action version bump before merging it.

Where this file and `DEVEL.md` disagree, `DEVEL.md` wins; correct this file in the same change.
